<title>NETHERLANDS: KLM shares up 5 pct on stake sale report.</title>
<headline>KLM shares up 5 pct on stake sale report.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in KLM rose over five percent or 3.20 guilders to 63.50 after a newspaper report said KLM was mulling the sale of its 19 percent stake in its U.S. affiliate Northwest Airlines.</p>
<p>Dealers said a sell-off of the stake would support KLM shares strongly because it would fetch a good price and open the way for closer operational ties with Northwest or alternative partners.</p>
<p>A KLM spokesman was not immediately available for comment on the front page article.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
